ens/colors#charts","content":"Charts"},"101":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-15","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#sidebar","content":"Sidebar"},"102":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-16","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#vital-extensions","content":"Vital Extensions"},"103":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-17","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#avatar-palette","content":"Avatar Palette"},"104":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-18","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#tag-palette","content":"Tag Palette"},"105":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-19","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#overview","content":"Vital Design follows the shadcn/ui\nnaming convention for its semantic layer. Colors are defined under\ntokens/ (Style Dictionary), built into src-v2/styles/tokens/generated.css\nas CSS custom properties on :root, and exposed to Tailwind via\n@theme inline (--color-*)."},"106":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-20","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#overview","content":"Primitive scales (--primary-50…900, --grayscale-100…900,\n--grayscale-opacity-100…900, --success-100…900, etc.) — internal\nfoundation. Reach for these when you need a specific shade for\ncharts, illustrations, or fine-grained tinting. Tailwind utility:\nbg-primary-500, text-grayscale-700, etc."},"107":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-21","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#overview","content":"Semantic tokens (--background, --primary, --card,\n--destructive, …) — the public API. These describe intent\nand pair with -foreground siblings for legible content on the\nsurface. Tailwind utility: bg-primary text-primary-foreground."},"108":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-22","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#overview","content":"Component tokens (--avatar-*-fg, --tag-*-solid) — closed\npalettes used by specific components."},"109":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-23","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#primary","content":"The primary palette is a blue scale used for interactive elements,\nbuttons, focus states, and key affordances."},"110":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-24","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#grayscale","content":"The default grayscale palette is fully solid — use it whenever the\nsurface must be opaque (popovers, tooltips, toasts, solid chips)."},"111":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-25","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#grayscale-opacity","content":"The opacity variant uses rgba(35, 35, 50, α) so it tonally adapts\nover any background. Use it for hover tints, dividers, disabled fields,\nand other states where translucency is desired. --grayscale-opacity-900\nis the only solid hex."},"112":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-26","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#success","content":"Positive feedback, confirmations, \"saved\" states."},"113":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-27","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#info","content":"Informational messaging and neutral status indicators."},"114":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-28","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#warning","content":"Caution states — soft warnings that don't block flow."},"115":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-2