ed components."},"646":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup-16","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup#registry-installed-local-components","content":"If your components.json points to a custom directory outside Tailwind's automatic source detection, add an @source rule that matches your local component path."},"647":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup-17","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup#design-tokens","content":"Registry installs expose the Vital Design design tokens as CSS custom properties and Tailwind utilities. The shadcn flow writes the required theme variables and the not-disabled custom variant into your configured global CSS file for you."},"648":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup-18","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup#design-tokens","content":"For example, the following tokens become available:"},"649":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup-19","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup#design-tokens","content":"These are exposed as Tailwind color utilities via @theme inline:"},"650":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup-20","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup#postcss-configuration","content":"Tailwind CSS 4 requires @tailwindcss/postcss. Create or update postcss.config.js (or postcss.config.cjs, depending on your project) like this:"},"651":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup-21","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/tailwind-setup#postcss-configuration","content":"If your project already uses autoprefixer, you can keep it."},"652":{"id":"/docs/getting-start